            <ArticleTitle>Kounis syndrome: myocardial infarction secondary to an allergic insult--a rare clinical entity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>559-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The association of an acute coronary syndrome with mast cell activation secondary to allergen exposure is known as the Kounis syndrome. We present two cases of the Kounis syndrome: (i) one was misdiagnosed as acute ST elevation myocardial infarction and treated with thrombolytics; (ii) the second diagnosis was made after a recurrence two months after the first incident.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
